      "Once upon a time Currentzis lived in Perm — and not just lived there, but worked on behalf of the people, trying to turn this backwater into a modern cultural centre. Others tried too, not everyone managed it — Currentzis did. He invited talent from abroad, organized events accessible to ordinary people, and the people grew better, more educated for it. Apparently that didn't sit well with someone, and the 'devil of Russian theatre' got sent off to St. Petersburg — the city of his own student years.",
