      "I understand it's all much more prosaic than that: someone couldn't agree on money, someone said something unpleasant at the wrong moment — this will always stay locked up seven ways. But it's nice, sometimes, to think that art isn't made for profit, even though, more often than not, everyone needs their cut — you can't exist without money after all. And it's easy to see why Currentzis is running concerts on such a massive scale right now: Dom Radio, where he stages his experiments, has to be maintained, the rent paid, the future thought about. And it does seem like, more or less, everyone ends up better off.",
